cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GradientMail: Distributed training through asynchronous message exchange"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Gabriel Francisco
    family-names: dos Santos Silva
    email: gabfssilva@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  GradientMail implements Decoupled DiLoCo over a shared mailbox: nodes exchange
  parameter fragments through S3, R2, MinIO or Hugging Face Storage Buckets,
  without P2P connections or a separate coordinator. Each learner wraps an
  existing PyTorch or MLX training loop, keeps a local copy of the model with
  its own optimizer, and publishes its update for one parameter fragment at a
  time on a staggered schedule. For each round, one of the training nodes is
  elected to merge the updates with RDA, apply the Nesterov outer step and
  commit the fragment through the mailbox; the other learners align with the
  commit, and another node takes over if the elected one fails. The cluster is
  heterogeneous and elastic: nodes with different GPUs and frameworks can join
  an ongoing run, train for a period and leave.
repository-code: "https://github.com/ppgsi-lab/gradientmail"
url: "https://ppgsi-lab.github.io/gradientmail/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - distributed-training
  - diloco
  - local-sgd
  - decentralized-training
  - object-storage
  - pytorch
  - mlx
